```

But what about `(AND hello)`: group → parseAdjacency → leading AND skipped → hello. Good. `AND hello` → TERM(hello). Good. `AND OR hello` → both skipped → hello. Fine.

Hmm, but leading-skip only at very start of parseAdjacency; inside a group after first clause can't happen (handled within parseOr). OK.

Alternatively more uniformly: skip those operators at the top of each loop iteration only when clauses.length===0. Same thing since after first iteration clauses non-empty. Keep simple version above.

Also check `OR hello` still works: parseAdjacency skips OR, then parseOr → hello. Good (before it worked via parseOr leading-skip).

